  "description": "What: the same sun-heated parked vehicle is NOT seen by thermal against hot bare ground (CE-1987, R-1058; docs/DESIGN_Thermal_And_Acoustic_Sensing.md \u00a79.2, \u00a79.7) \u2014 the crossover is a property of the PAIR. On basic-desert (bare ground) at 13:36 local (solar ~12:30), clear sky: 'Observer' (TKB 215, 4 K) at (50, 300); 'Soil Tank', a T-72 parked with its engine OFF, at (450, 300), 400 m east. Judge: the hull and the sun-baked ground are within the sight's 4 K, so the observer's memory never carries the THERMAL bit for it (his eyes may still see it in daylight). Fail: a thermal bit. Red-proof: the background read as grass everywhere and the hull stands out. Its sibling th-hull-in-the-sun holds the other half.",
